.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_PCP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_pcp_new ,
.Nm mbt_pcp_free ,
.Nm mbt_pcp_map ,
.Nm mbt_pcp_unmap ,
.Nm mbt_pcp_external_addr ,
.Nm mbt_pcp_external_port
.Nd PCP implementation for BitTorrent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/pcp.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
PCP (Port Control Protocol) is used to request port mappings from a gateway
(e.g., a router). This implementation provides an interface for managing these
mappings within the MBT event loop.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_new "struct mbt_pcp **out" "struct mbt_ev *ev" "const char *gateway"
creates a new PCP client. The
.Fa gateway
parameter specifies the gateway to use; if
.Fa NULL ,
the implementation attempts to auto-detect the default gateway.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_free "struct mbt_pcp *p"
destroys the PCP client and cleans up any associated resources.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_map "struct mbt_pcp *p" "uint8_t protocol" "uint16_t internal_port" "uint32_t lifetime" "mbt_pcp_cb cb" "void *arg"
requests a port mapping for the specified protocol and internal port. It handles
retransmission of requests and automatic renewal of mappings. The
.Fa cb
callback is invoked when the mapping is successfully established or renewed,
providing the external address, external port, lifetime, and user-provided
argument.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_unmap "struct mbt_pcp *p" "uint8_t protocol" "uint16_t internal_port"
requests the deletion of an existing port mapping for the specified protocol
and internal port.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_external_addr "struct mbt_pcp *p"
returns the external IP address currently assigned to the PCP client's
mapping. Returns
.Fa NULL
if no active mapping exists.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pcp_external_port "struct mbt_pcp *p"
returns the external port number currently assigned to the PCP client's
mapping. Returns 0 if no active mapping exists.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Example of requesting a UDP port mapping:
.Bd -literal
struct mbt_ev *ev;
struct mbt_pcp *pcp;
mbt_pcp_new(&pcp, ev, NULL);

void my_cb(const char *addr, uint16_t port, uint32_t lifetime, void *arg) {
    printf("extern: %s:%u\n", addr, port);
}

mbt_pcp_map(pcp, IPPROTO_UDP, 6881, 3600, my_cb, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_session 3
